# What lands in the SOURCE distribution (`python -m build --sdist`).
#
# This does not affect the wheel -- the artefact `pip install solver-support`
# actually fetches -- which carries only the solver_support package and its
# metadata, and is already minimal. It governs the source release, which should
# be self-contained: buildable, and testable by anyone repackaging it (a distro
# or conda-forge recipe typically runs the suite at build time).
#
# setuptools' defaults already pick up README.md, LICENSE, pyproject.toml and
# tests/test_*.py -- but NOT tests/conftest.py, whose name does not match
# `test*`, nor the YAML fixture the registry tests load. The sdist therefore
# shipped a test suite that could not run at all: every test needing a fixture
# errored on a missing one. These two lines are what make it coherent.
recursive-include tests *.py *.yaml

# The docs the README points at, so the source release does not dangle links to
# files it does not carry.
recursive-include docs *.md
